boyko parity patch for Jolt's PerformanceTest (physics perf campaign, plan section 1: H3, H8, H10, O5; v2: lane DYN-SCENES).
The v1 hunks apply with `git apply` to Jolt v5.3.0 and v5.6.0 (checked 2026-09-19); the v2 hunks, the dynamic parity
scenes, are checked on v5.6.0 only (2026-10-06: the comparison is against Jolt 5.6 alone).
Build recipe, flags and what each change is for: the header of ../jolt_parity_pyramid.rs, "Build (Jolt)".

  PyramidScene.h         damping 0 (boyko has no rigid-body damping); mAllowSleeping from SetAllowSleeping;
                         v2: namespace BoykoDyn (the programs, an independent C++ derivation of boyko's
                         dyn_spec.rs) and BoykoDynPyramidScene (J-T plus a program, events in ApplyEvents)
  PerformanceTestScene.h SetAllowSleeping, false for every scene that does not support it;
                         v2: BoykoDynLog and ApplyEvents, called before each step's clock starts
  PerformanceTest.cpp    -no_pair_cache, -allow_sleep (+ an Active Bodies column in -f's CSV),
                         -receipt (a counting ContactListener: receipt_<quality>_th<N>.csv),
                         and one "boyko-parity-patch v1" line naming the options in force (unchanged by v2);
                         v2: -dyn=kick|shoot|slide, -sanity, -scene_dump=, -pose_out=, -spawn_pose_out=, a second
                         "boyko-parity-dyn v1" line printed only with them, Update's error flags kept and counted

